        "- **Mispriced options**: If implied volatility is estimated from an overfit model, options will be systematically overpriced or underpriced relative to fair value, creating arbitrage losses\n",
        "- **Failed hedges**: Delta and vega hedges computed from overfit models will be wrong when market conditions change, leaving the desk exposed\n",
        "- **False confidence**: High in-sample $R^2$ misleads risk managers into believing the model is robust when it is not\n",
        "- **Regulatory risk**: Overfit VaR models underestimate tail risk, potentially breaching regulatory capital requirements\n",
